 HISTORY:
 ~~~~~~~~
  V0.1  11-07-92 - Internal Version

  V1.0  02-03-93 - Release Version

  V1.1  03-20-93 - Added The 2 OutputList Option
                 - Added Support for .txt.gr Files
                 - [Bulls.CFG CHANGED!]

  V1.2  05-05-93 - Added 'Non-Stop' Menu Showing, if you got too many Bulls
                   then the irritating 'More (Y/n/ns)' appeared... FIXED
                 - Cleaned Up.
        06-21-93 - Fixed a small Error found with the RexxDoorDebugger.

  V2.0ß 01-01-94 - ReWritten to XIM!
        01-13-94 - Better Bulls.CFG reading
                 - Added some more Ansi Colors
                 - Changed the Bulls.CFG layout (same layout as JoinCnf.CFG).
                   It's now also possible to use your Own Bulletin Logo
                   [Bulls.CFG CHANGED!]
        01-14-94 - Bug Report from JPS
                    o When using Bull [00] it was possible to press different
                      <SHIFT>-keys to show it.. FIXED
        01-17-94 - When Bulls is run, it will ShowUp on the Server.
        01-25-94 - Fixed the '10-Node' BUG

  V2.0  01-29-94 - Release

  V2.1ß 02-05-94 - Change the 'Full Use of 80 Chars/Line' to 79 Chars/Line
                   because some Terminals on Amiga/PC can't handle the 80th
                   character right (extra linefeeds)!
        02-07-94 - Bug Report from B.O.B/CF & Enzo:
                    o When using NON-Ansi the character color will change to
                      Magenta when exiting/using Bulls.
                      There were 2 ESC-chars after eachother in the command-
                      line which /X doesn't like... FIXED!
        02-28-94 - Added Cursor-Key Support. To Include this the Bulls.CFG
                   changed:
                    o Bull0.txt support has been deleted, so change your
                      Bull-Access!
                 - [Bulls.CFG CHANGED!]
        03-20-94 - Optimized some code.
        03-24-94 - Added some Suggestions from SpeedDevil/Partek:
                    o When starting Bulls the BullSelection >[]< will now
                      be disabled until an ArrowKey is pressed or a Bull is 
                      selected.
                    o After showing a Bulletin pressing <ENTER> will show
                      the Bulletin-List again and not Quit Bulls anymore.
                      So it's now only possible to Quit Bulls in the
                      Bulletin-List.
 
  V2.1  04-13-94 - Release Version.

  V2.2ß 04-18-94 - ReCompiled with the Latest AE.Includes.
        04-24-94 - Fixed the Text-Showing Error when there is no ClearScreen
                   code in the Bulletin.
        05-21-94 - Changed a few things:
                    when a bulletin is selected from command line (b 1) then
                    Bulls will quit right away (when the bulletin doesn't
                    exist the Bulls menu will be shown)
                 - Removed a small bug concerning the Commandline starting.
                 - Killed all sscanf's in the Source coz of Bugs in the
                   SAS Compiler and this way Bulls gets 2 kb smaller!
        06-21-94 - When a Bulletin is shown then the shown BulletinNr will be
                   printed on the commandline (Request from Tycoon)
                 - BugFix: When there where no Bulletins present in the
                   current Conference it was still possible to enter a key.

  V2.2  07-01-94 - Release Version.


